==English==

===Alternative spellings===
*[[pandar]]

===Etymology===
From Chaucer's character {{term|w:Pandarus|Pandare}} (in ''[[w:Troilus and Criseyde|Troilus and Criseyde]]''), from {{It.}} {{term|w:Pandarus|Pandaro}} (found in [[w:Boccaccio|Boccaccio]]), from {{L.}} {{term|w:Pandarus|Pandarus}}, from {{AGr.}} {{term|Πάνδαρος|sc=polytonic}}. (See also Shakespeare's [[wikibooks:Troilus and Cressida|Troilus and Cressida]])

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|/ˈpandə/}}, (''RP'') {{IPA|/ˈpændə/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˈpændɚ/}}, {{SAMPA|/"p{nd@`/}}
* {{audio|en-us-pander.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A person who furthers the [[illicit]] love-affairs of others; a [[pimp]] or [[procurer]], especially when male. (Later [[panderer]].)
# An offer of illicit [[sex]] with a third party.
# An illicit or illegal [[offer]], usually to [[tempt]].

